        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(status): report skipped channel credential checks accurately",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nFast `openclaw status` now threads `credentialResolutionSkipped` into the shared\nchannel summary path so configured SecretRef-backed channels can say\n`credential not checked` instead of the misleading\n`secret unavailable in this command path`.\n\nThis follow-up fixes the last boundary bug in that change: when\n`executeStatusScanFromOverview()` was called without a `summary` object, it\nstill passed `credentialResolutionSkipped: undefined` into\n`resolveStatusSummaryFromOverview()`. The adjacent execute test does an exact\nobject match, so `check-test-types`/test compilation surfaced the mismatch even\nthough the runtime behavior was otherwise fine.\n\nThe fix keeps the new flag propagation, but omits the key entirely when the\nvalue is `undefined`.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs run src/commands/status.scan-execute.test.ts src/commands/status.summary.test.ts src/infra/channel-summary.test.ts`\n  - `Test Files  3 passed (3)`\n  - `Tests  23 passed (23)`\n\n## Real behavior proof\n\n- **Behavior addressed:**\n  Fast-status shared channel summary output now uses the skipped-probe wording\n  `credential not checked` for configured Slack HTTP credentials when local\n  credential resolution is intentionally skipped.\n\n- **Real environment tested:**\n  Local OpenClaw source checkout on macOS, rebased on latest `upstream/main`.\n\n- **Exact steps or command run after this patch:**\n\n```bash\nnode scripts/run-vitest.mjs run \\\n  src/commands/status.scan-execute.test.ts \\\n  src/commands/status.summary.test.ts \\\n  src/infra/channel-summary.test.ts\n```\n\n- **Evidence after fix:**\n\n```text\nTest Files  3 passed (3)\nTests  23 passed (23)\n```\n\nFocused channel-summary regression:\n\n```text\nuses credential-not-checked wording when fast status skips credential resolution\n  - primary (Primary) (bot:config, signing:config, credential not checked)\n```\n\n- **Observed result after fix:**\n  The execute wrapper now conditionally omits `credentialResolutionSkipped` when\n  it is undefined, the fast-status scan passes the skip flag into shared channel\n  summaries, and the shared summary path renders `credential not checked`.\n\n- **What was not tested:**\n  No live `openclaw status` CLI run against a configured gateway; no committed\n  proof scripts.",
